    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #350\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed branch `bb/relay-142-auth-v1-05-08-implement-single-use-pas-thr_8v5qpi8wxw` to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements single-use password recovery over SMTP (issue #142):\n\n- **Migration** `0027_password_reset_tokens.sql`: new `password_reset_tokens` table (user FK, unique `token_hash`, `expires_at`, `consumed_at`, `created_at`), mirroring `sessions.token_hash`'s \"only the hash persists\" pattern.\n- **`passwordResetStore.ts`**: DB access, including `consumePasswordResetToken` — a single atomic `UPDATE ... WHERE consumed_at IS NULL AND expires_at > now() RETURNING` that both requires and marks single-use consumption in one statement, closing the double-consume race.\n- **`passwordResetActions.ts`**: `requestPasswordReset` (resolves identically for a known and an unknown email — no disclosure of account existence; generates a high-entropy token and emails a reset link only for a real account) and `resetPassword` (atomic consume, new Argon2id hash, deterministic `PasswordResetTokenError` reason of `invalid`/`expired`/`consumed`).\n- **`passwordResetMail.ts`**: a new app-level SMTP mailer (`NodemailerPasswordResetMailer`), reusing the SMTP infrastructure pattern from #27, independent of the per-mailbox draft/Sent-folder workflow (which doesn't apply to a system notification with no owning mailbox item).\n- **HTTP surface** in `authHandler.ts`: `POST /api/auth/password-reset/request` and `POST /api/auth/password-reset/consume`, wired into `serve.ts` with `APP_BASE_URL`/`SMTP_*` env config (falls back to a `noop` mailer that throws if SMTP isn't configured, rather than silently pretending to send).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: 114 passed\n- [x] Integration tests (real Postgres): 722 passed, including new coverage for token issuance/consumption, expiry, reuse rejection, and email-existence non-disclosure\n- [x] E2E tests: 5 passed\n- [x] Lint clean\n- [x] Full workspace `tsc` build clean\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
