    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #350\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nWorking tree was clean; the review-response commit (`210ac66`) has been pushed.\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-142-auth-v1-05-08-implement-single-use-pas-thr_8v5qpi8wxw`\n\nThis push addresses the code-review findings on PR #350:\n- **High**: `resetPassword` now revokes every other active session for the user in the same transaction as the password write, so a session an attacker held before the reset can't outlive it.\n- **Medium**: `requestPasswordReset` now caps reset-token issuance per account to 3 per rolling hour, silently no-op'ing past the cap (same response shape as an unknown email), preventing reset-email flooding.\n- **Low**: the reset URL is now HTML-escaped in the emailed HTML body as defense in depth.\n\nAdded test coverage for the session-revocation and rate-limiting behavior. Build, lint, unit (114/114), integration (727/727), and e2e (5/5) all pass on this commit.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
