    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #350\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nWorking tree was clean; pushed the pending commit (`bc7b305`).\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-142-auth-v1-05-08-implement-single-use-pas-thr_8v5qpi8wxw`\n\nThis push resolves the medium-severity correctness finding from the latest review of PR #350: `resetPassword`'s signature previously accepted `Pool | PoolClient`, but its consume-token/update-password/revoke-sessions sequence is only atomic inside a caller-managed transaction — a bare `Pool` would auto-commit each statement independently, risking a token being consumed without the password actually changing on a later failure. The signature is now narrowed to `PoolClient` only, forcing every caller into a transaction (the HTTP handler already did this via `withTransaction`); the tests were updated to do the same.\n\nBuild, lint, unit (114/114), integration (727/727), and e2e (5/5) all pass on this commit.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
